<title>SINGAPORE: India offers Bombay Feb 20-22 low aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India offers Bombay Feb 20-22 low aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has offered through a tender 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting February 20-22 from Bombay on the Indian west coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on February 5 and is valid until February 6.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN tender from Bombay, lifting January 23-25, was awarded at $25.38 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
